{%- comment -%}
  Canva-style live layout editor for the compare tile section.

  It turns the "See how Core upgrades your experience" block into a
  drag-and-drop canvas: click any tile / image / text / icon to select
  it, drag to move it, and drag a corner (or scroll the wheel) to make
  it bigger or smaller — just like moving elements around a Canva page.

  HOW IT TURNS ON
    Add ?edit=1 to the product-page URL in the theme preview. That flips
    the section into edit mode AND remembers it (so it stays on across
    reloads while you fine-tune). Add ?edit=0 (or hit "Done") to leave.
    Normal visitors never see any of this — with no flag, the script only
    re-applies a saved layout and adds zero controls.

  HOW "LOCK IT" WORKS
    Your moves are saved live in the browser (localStorage) so nothing is
    lost on reload and the preview always shows your work-in-progress.
    When it's positioned how you want, click "Copy layout" (or just tell
    Claude "lock it") and hand Claude the copied code — Claude bakes those
    exact positions/sizes permanently into the desktop CSS and clears the
    temporary browser copy.

  This is a desktop tool: the compare grid only uses its big scaled
  layout at >=900px, so the editor's handles only appear there.

  ALIGN
    Click "Align" to snap small accidental drift (up to 14px, or 40px
    with Shift+click) on a tile back to its perfect grid position —
    or, if nothing is selected, straightens every tile at once.
    Deliberate larger moves are left alone.

    Tiles snap to whichever of the 6 grid slots they're now CLOSEST
    to, on both axes — not just back to their own original slot. So
    to swap two tiles: drag each roughly into the other's spot, then
    click Align, and both lock exactly into place. This works because
    a tile's real grid cell (its layout position) never actually moves
    when it's dragged — only its on-screen transform does — so all 6
    real slots are always known and available to snap to.

    Align touches a tile's own position/size, and a text box's (a
    caption, heading, or the big stat number) horizontal position —
    small drift only, up to the same threshold, and text is never
    moved vertically or resized by Align (its vertical spot is set by
    its own CSS on purpose). Everything else that lives inside a tile
    — an image or an icon — is left alone entirely: once placed, it
    stays exactly where it's put, since a deliberate small nudge on a
    photo shouldn't keep getting silently reverted just because Align
    ran.

  EDITING TEXT
    Double-click a caption/heading (not the live numbers, which are
    computed by JS) to drill into it — same as any image or icon, and
    still draggable with a single click-hold from there. Once it's
    selected, either press Enter or just click it again (a plain click
    that doesn't turn into a drag) to start typing into it, in its own
    font; the cursor lands at the end of the existing text so you can
    add more. Press Enter again to start a new line lower in the same
    box. Click anywhere else (or press Escape) to stop typing; the
    edit is saved live like everything else and included in "Copy
    layout".

    Click-to-type only fires on a SECOND click, once the text is
    already selected — the double-click that first drills into/selects
    it always just selects, so it's still possible to double-click and
    immediately drag without getting hijacked into typing.

    With a text box selected (not currently being typed into), press
    Backspace or Delete to clear it out.

  UNDO
    Click "Undo" in the toolbar to step back one action at a time —
    a move, a resize, typing/deleting a caption, or a whole Align /
    Reset click. Holding an arrow key or scrolling to resize counts as
    ONE action (the whole hold/scroll), not one per tick.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .cv-tb{position:fixed;top:14px;left:14px;z-index:2147483000;display:flex;gap:6px;align-items:center;
    background:#111;color:#fff;border:1px solid #2c2c2c;border-radius:12px;padding:8px 10px;
    font:13px/1.2 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
    box-shadow:0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.35);user-select:none;}
  .cv-tb__dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#16c76a;box-shadow:0 0 8px #16c76a;flex:none;}
  .cv-tb__title{font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.02em;margin-right:4px;}
  .cv-tb__hint{opacity:.55;font-size:11px;max-width:280px;line-height:1.35;}
  .cv-btn{appearance:none;border:1px solid #333;background:#1d1d1f;color:#fff;border-radius:8px;
    padding:6px 10px;font:inherit;font-size:12px;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap;}
  .cv-btn:hover{background:#2a2a2c;}
  .cv-btn--go{background:#0a84ff;border-color:#0a84ff;}
  .cv-btn--go:hover{background:#0a74e0;}

  .cv-hover{outline:1.5px dashed rgba(10,132,255,.55) !important;outline-offset:1px;cursor:grab;}
  /* The image wrappers are normally pointer-events:none (they're decorative,
     aria-hidden) so clicks pass through to the tile behind them. While
     editing, re-enable pointer events on them so the image itself is
     clickable/double-clickable like everything else. */
  .cv-editing .pdp-cmp__img-slot,
  .cv-editing .pdp-cmp__img-slot img{pointer-events:auto !important;}
  /* Kill the browser's OWN pinch-zoom and double-tap-zoom document-wide
     while editing — without this, a two-finger pinch (meant to resize the
     selected element) and a double-tap (meant to drill into it) both also
     trigger the browser's native page-zoom at the same time, and once that
     kicks in its own momentum/rubber-band settling is what actually reads
     as an image "flying off" after you let go — our JS was never adding
     any drift of its own. pan-y keeps normal one-finger vertical page
     scroll working everywhere; it only removes zoom gestures. */
  html.cv-editing{touch-action:pan-y;}
  .cv-box{position:fixed;z-index:2147482000;border:1.5px solid #0a84ff;pointer-events:none;
    box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.6);}
  .cv-h{position:absolute;width:12px;height:12px;background:#fff;border:1.5px solid #0a84ff;
    border-radius:50%;pointer-events:auto;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}
  .cv-h--tl{top:-7px;left:-7px;cursor:nwse-resize;}
  .cv-h--tr{top:-7px;right:-7px;cursor:nesw-resize;}
  .cv-h--bl{bottom:-7px;left:-7px;cursor:nesw-resize;}
  .cv-h--br{bottom:-7px;right:-7px;cursor:nwse-resize;}
  .cv-tag{position:absolute;top:-22px;left:-1px;background:#0a84ff;color:#fff;font:11px/1 -apple-system,
    BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;padding:3px 6px;border-radius:5px;white-space:nowrap;
    pointer-events:none;}
  .cv-editing-text{outline:2px solid #0a84ff !important;outline-offset:2px;cursor:text !important;
    /* Only an explicit Enter (a <br> we insert ourselves) should start a
       new line — without this, the browser's own auto-wrap kicks in as
       soon as typed text exceeds the box width, which looks like the
       line broke on its own. */
    white-space:nowrap !important;}

  .cv-panel{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:2147483100;background:rgba(0,0,0,.55);display:none;
    align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:24px;}
  .cv-panel.is-open{display:flex;}
  .cv-panel__card{background:#161617;color:#fff;border:1px solid #2c2c2c;border-radius:14px;
    width:min(640px,100%);max-height:80vh;display:flex;flex-direction:column;overflow:hidden;
    font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;box-shadow:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.5);}
  .cv-panel__head{padding:14px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #262628;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;}
  .cv-panel__head b{font-size:14px;}
  .cv-panel textarea{width:100%;flex:1;min-height:220px;border:0;background:#0d0d0e;color:#d6d6d8;
    font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;padding:14px 16px;resize:none;box-sizing:border-box;}
  .cv-panel__foot{padding:12px 16px;border-top:1px solid #262628;display:flex;gap:8px;justify-content:flex-end;align-items:center;}
  .cv-panel__note{margin-right:auto;opacity:.6;font-size:11px;max-width:340px;}

  /* ---- phone: dock the toolbar to the bottom, let it wrap, and make the
     corner resize handles finger-sized (the 12px desktop dots are too
     small to grab with a fingertip). Kept to coarse pointers so a
     touchscreen laptop with a mouse still gets the compact desktop UI. */
  @media (max-width:899px) and (pointer:coarse){
    .cv-tb{top:auto;bottom:calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));left:8px;right:8px;
      flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;padding:10px;gap:8px;}
    .cv-tb__title{margin-right:0;}
    .cv-tb__hint{flex-basis:100%;max-width:none;text-align:center;order:9;font-size:11px;}
    .cv-btn{padding:10px 13px;font-size:13px;}
    .cv-h{width:22px;height:22px;}
    .cv-h--tl{top:-12px;left:-12px;} .cv-h--tr{top:-12px;right:-12px;}
    .cv-h--bl{bottom:-12px;left:-12px;} .cv-h--br{bottom:-12px;right:-12px;}
    .cv-tag{top:-24px;font-size:12px;padding:4px 7px;}
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.__cvCanvaInit) return;
  window.__cvCanvaInit = true;

  var qs = location.search || '';
  var wantOn  = /[?&]edit=1(?:&|$)/.test(qs);
  var wantOff = /[?&]edit=0(?:&|$)/.test(qs);
  function ls(get, k, v){ try { return get ? localStorage.getItem(k) : localStorage.setItem(k, v); } catch(e){ return null; } }
  function rm(k){ try { localStorage.removeItem(k); } catch(e){} }

  if (wantOn)  ls(false, 'volt-canva-on', '1');
  if (wantOff) rm('volt-canva-on');
  var ON = ls(true, 'volt-canva-on') === '1' && !wantOff;

  var LKEY = 'volt-canva-layout-4';
  var layout = {};
  try { layout = JSON.parse(ls(true, LKEY) || '{}') || {}; } catch(e){ layout = {}; }

  var EDITABLE = '.pdp-cmp__card, .pdp-cmp__img-slot img, .pdp-cmp__eyebrow, ' +
    '.pdp-cmp__stat, .pdp-cmp__stat-row, .pdp-cmp__sub, ' +
    '.pdp-cmp__battery-icon, .pdp-cmp__select-heading, .pdp-cmp__label, .pdp-cmp__select-wrap, ' +
    // The visible "×" on the partial-charges tile ("Up to 3.6× / 20% to
    // 80%") is its own span so it can be grabbed on its own, separate from
    // the number — but its hidden mirror twin (used to balance the
    // centering) is aria-hidden and must stay out of reach.
    '.pdp-cmp__stat-x:not(.pdp-cmp__stat-x--mirror)';

  function start(){
    var root = document.querySelector('.pdp-cmp');
    if (!root) return;

    function pathFor(el){
      var parts = [], cur = el;
      while (cur && cur !== root && cur.parentNode){
        var p = cur.parentNode;
        var idx = Array.prototype.indexOf.call(p.children, cur) + 1;
        parts.unshift(':nth-child(' + idx + ')');
        cur = p;
      }
      return parts.join('>');
    }
    // Only literal captions are safe to type into — the stat numbers
    // (data-calc-*) are computed live by the compare script, so editing
    // them by hand would just get overwritten on the next recalculation.
    function isTextEditable(el){
      return el.matches('.pdp-cmp__eyebrow, .pdp-cmp__sub, .pdp-cmp__select-heading, .pdp-cmp__label');
    }
    // Wider than isTextEditable: also covers the big live-computed stat
    // numbers (e.g. "67h"), which must NOT be made typeable (they're
    // overwritten by the compare script on recalculation) but still
    // deserve the same "Align only ever straightens left/right, never
    // moves vertically" treatment as a caption.
    function isAlignHoriz(el){
      return isTextEditable(el) || el.matches('.pdp-cmp__stat, .pdp-cmp__stat-row');
    }

    var editingEl = null;

    function stateOf(el){
      var s = layout[el.__cvKey];
      return s ? {dx:s.dx||0, dy:s.dy||0, s:s.s||1, text:(s.text!=null ? s.text : null)} : {dx:0,dy:0,s:1,text:null};
    }

    // ---- carry a desktop-authored move onto whatever viewport is showing ----
    // Every drag is authored on desktop (the editor's controls only appear at
    // >=900px), so dx/dy are stored in the element's DESKTOP local pixels —
    // where a tile's untransformed box is DESK_REF_W wide. Mobile lays the
    // same tile out at its full column width (no scale transform), so a raw
    // desktop offset would land a caption/image in completely the wrong spot.
    // Since dx/tileWidth is the move as a fraction of its tile — and that
    // fraction is exactly what should look identical on both — we re-express
    // the offset for the current viewport as dx * (thisTileWidth / DESK_REF_W).
    // offsetWidth ignores transforms, so this measures true local box widths
    // and self-corrects to any phone width, not just one hard-coded size.
    // scale(s) is a unitless ratio and needs no conversion; the element's own
    // base transform is read per-viewport already, so it's right on each.
    var desktopMQ = window.matchMedia('(min-width:900px)');
    // Desktop's tile box width is fixed regardless of window size (its scale
    // transform does the sizing), so measure it once on desktop and cache it;
    // on a phone (no editor, only a restored layout) fall back to the cached
    // value, or the known baked default if this browser never saw desktop.
    var REFKEY = 'volt-canva-refw';
    var DESK_REF_W = (function(){
      if (desktopMQ.matches){
        var t = document.querySelector('.pdp-cmp__card');
        if (t && t.offsetWidth){ ls(false, REFKEY, String(t.offsetWidth)); return t.offsetWidth; }
      }
      var cached = parseFloat(ls(true, REFKEY));
      return cached > 0 ? cached : 107;
    })();
    function effTranslate(el, st){
      if (desktopMQ.matches) return {dx: st.dx, dy: st.dy};   // author viewport: verbatim
      // A whole tile moved onto a different desktop grid cell has no meaning
      // in mobile's single-column stack (that reordering is handled in CSS),
      // so don't fling the tile across the screen — only its contents move.
      if (el.matches('.pdp-cmp__card')) return {dx: 0, dy: 0};
      var tile = el.closest('.pdp-cmp__card');
      if (!tile || !tile.offsetWidth || !DESK_REF_W) return {dx: st.dx, dy: st.dy};
      var f = tile.offsetWidth / DESK_REF_W;
      return {dx: st.dx * f, dy: st.dy * f};
    }

    function applyState(el){
      var st = stateOf(el);
      var mv = effTranslate(el, st);
      var extra = '';
      if (mv.dx || mv.dy) extra += 'translate(' + mv.dx + 'px,' + mv.dy + 'px) ';
      if (st.s && st.s !== 1) extra += 'scale(' + st.s + ') ';
      // Base must come FIRST (outermost-applied last, i.e. leftmost in the
      // CSS list is applied outermost... concretely: composing as
      // "base extra" rather than "extra base" keeps a translate-type base
      // (e.g. a centering translateX(-50%) baked in from the element's own
      // CSS) from getting multiplied by the user's own scale(s) — which is
      // what silently drags an element off-center the more it's resized.
      // !important: once something's been baked (lock it), its position
      // lives in the stylesheet as an !important rule (needed there to
      // beat other, unrelated !important rules on some elements) — a
      // plain inline style can never outrank that, so dragging/resizing
      // anything already baked would silently do nothing. An inline
      // !important is the one thing that outranks an external !important.
      el.style.setProperty('transform', (el.__cvBase + ' ' + extra).trim(), 'important');
      if (el.__cvTextEditable){
        // Never touch innerHTML of the box currently being typed into —
        // that would reset the cursor mid-keystroke. Otherwise it should
        // always show whatever's saved, OR its original text if nothing
        // is — that "OR" matters for undo: undoing a delete (or a typed
        // edit) clears the saved text, and the box needs to actively come
        // back to its original content, not just sit however it was left.
        var wantText = st.text != null ? st.text : el.__cvOrigText;
        if (el !== editingEl && el.innerHTML !== wantText){
          el.innerHTML = wantText;
        }
        // Once a caption has been retyped, it should ONLY break where an
        // explicit Enter placed a <br> — never on its own just because the
        // line got long. Without this, editing was WYSIWYG only while the
        // box was focused; the instant you clicked away, the box fell back
        // to normal word-wrap and text you never broke could still jump to
        // a new line. Keep this on permanently (not just while editing)
        // for any box that's actually been retyped; leave untouched boxes
        // exactly as designed.
        el.style.whiteSpace = st.text != null ? 'nowrap' : '';
      }
    }
    function saveState(el, st){
      var noTransform = !st.dx && !st.dy && (!st.s || st.s === 1);
      var noText = st.text == null || (el.__cvTextEditable && st.text === el.__cvOrigText);
      if (noTransform && noText) delete layout[el.__cvKey];
      else {
        var entry = {dx:Math.round(st.dx*100)/100, dy:Math.round(st.dy*100)/100, s:Math.round(st.s*10000)/10000};
        if (!noText) entry.text = st.text;
        layout[el.__cvKey] = entry;
      }
      ls(false, LKEY, JSON.stringify(layout));
      applyState(el);
    }
    function saveText(el){
      var st = stateOf(el);
      st.text = el.innerHTML;
      saveState(el, st);
    }

    // ---- undo: one entry per user action (a drag, a resize, a type, an
    // Align/Reset click, a delete) — NOT one per intermediate saveState
    // call, or a single drag would take dozens of undos to unwind. Call
    // captureBatch() with the element(s) about to change BEFORE changing
    // them, do the change(s), then commitBatch() — it only pushes to
    // history if something in the batch actually ended up different.
    var history = [];
    var HISTORY_MAX = 50;
    function cloneEntry(e){ return e ? JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(e)) : null; }
    function captureBatch(elsArr){
      return elsArr.map(function(el){ return { el: el, prev: cloneEntry(layout[el.__cvKey]) }; });
    }
    function commitBatch(batch){
      var changed = batch.filter(function(b){
        return JSON.stringify(b.prev) !== JSON.stringify(layout[b.el.__cvKey] || null);
      });
      if (!changed.length) return;
      history.push(changed);
      if (history.length > HISTORY_MAX) history.shift();
    }
    function undo(){
      if (!history.length) return;
      var batch = history.pop();
      batch.forEach(function(b){
        if (b.prev) layout[b.el.__cvKey] = b.prev; else delete layout[b.el.__cvKey];
        applyState(b.el);
      });
      ls(false, LKEY, JSON.stringify(layout));
      positionBox();
    }

    // Register every editable element: record its base transform + stable key,
    // then re-apply any saved layout (this runs even when NOT editing).
    var els = [].slice.call(root.querySelectorAll(EDITABLE));
    els.forEach(function(el){
      var cs = getComputedStyle(el).transform;
      el.__cvBase = (cs && cs !== 'none') ? cs : '';
      el.__cvKey  = pathFor(el);
      el.__cvTextEditable = isTextEditable(el);
      el.__cvAlignH = isAlignHoriz(el);
      el.__cvOrigText = el.__cvTextEditable ? el.innerHTML : null;
      applyState(el);
    });

    // Crossing the 900px line (e.g. dragging the window narrow to check the
    // phone layout, or a device rotating) swaps every element's base
    // transform and its tile width, so re-apply the saved moves against the
    // new viewport — otherwise a desktop-scaled offset would linger on the
    // mobile layout until a full reload.
    (desktopMQ.addEventListener ? desktopMQ.addEventListener('change', reapplyAll)
                                : desktopMQ.addListener(reapplyAll));
    function reapplyAll(){
      els.forEach(function(el){
        // el.style.transform is our own inline output; strip it first so the
        // freshly-read base is the element's real CSS for this viewport, not
        // last viewport's composed result.
        el.style.transform = '';
        var cs = getComputedStyle(el).transform;
        el.__cvBase = (cs && cs !== 'none') ? cs : '';
        applyState(el);
      });
    }

    if (!ON) return;                 // viewer with a saved layout — no controls

    // Editor controls run on phones too now (touch handlers added below).
    // Whether the compare block is in its big scaled desktop layout or the
    // stacked mobile one, all the drag/resize math is viewport-agnostic:
    // it divides screen-pixel deltas by the element's cumulative ancestor
    // scale (cumScale), which is ~4.35x on desktop and ~1x on mobile, so a
    // drag lands 1:1 either way.
    var coarse = window.matchMedia('(pointer:coarse)').matches;

    document.documentElement.classList.add('cv-editing');

    // Cumulative scale of an element's ANCESTOR chain (excludes the element's
    // own transform). A screen-pixel drag delta divided by this gives the
    // delta in the element's own local coordinate units.
    function cumScale(el){
      var sx = 1, sy = 1, n = el.parentNode;
      while (n && n.nodeType === 1){
        var t = getComputedStyle(n).transform;
        if (t && t !== 'none'){
          try { var m = new DOMMatrixReadOnly(t); sx *= m.a; sy *= m.d; } catch(e){}
        }
        n = n.parentNode;
      }
      return {sx: sx || 1, sy: sy || 1};
    }
    function centerOf(el){ var r = el.getBoundingClientRect(); return {x:r.left+r.width/2, y:r.top+r.height/2}; }

    // ---- selection overlay ----
    var box = document.createElement('div'); box.className = 'cv-box'; box.style.display = 'none';
    var tag = document.createElement('div'); tag.className = 'cv-tag'; box.appendChild(tag);
    ['tl','tr','bl','br'].forEach(function(c){
      var h = document.createElement('div'); h.className = 'cv-h cv-h--' + c; h.dataset.corner = c; box.appendChild(h);
    });
    document.body.appendChild(box);

    var sel = null;
    function label(el){
      if (el.matches('.pdp-cmp__card')) return 'tile';
      if (el.tagName === 'IMG') return 'image';
      if (el.matches('.pdp-cmp__select-heading')) return 'heading';
      if (el.matches('.pdp-cmp__select-wrap')) return 'selector';
      if (el.matches('.pdp-cmp__battery-icon')) return 'icon';
      if (el.matches('.pdp-cmp__stat-x')) return '×';
      return 'text';
    }
    function positionBox(){
      if (!sel){ box.style.display = 'none'; return; }
      var r = sel.getBoundingClientRect();
      box.style.display = 'block';
      box.style.left = r.left + 'px'; box.style.top = r.top + 'px';
      box.style.width = r.width + 'px'; box.style.height = r.height + 'px';
    }
    // On touch, the selected element gets touch-action:none so a finger
    // drag ON it moves it instead of scrolling the page — every OTHER
    // element keeps normal touch-action, so you can still scroll the tall
    // tile stack by dragging anywhere that isn't the current selection.
    // (Inline touch-action is inert for mouse, so this is a no-op on
    // desktop.)
    function select(el){
      if (sel && sel !== el && sel.style) sel.style.touchAction = '';
      sel = el;
      if (el && el.style) el.style.touchAction = 'none';
      tag.textContent = label(el); positionBox();
    }
    function deselect(){ if (sel && sel.style) sel.style.touchAction = ''; sel = null; positionBox(); }

    // ---- inline text editing ----
    var textEditBatch = null;
    function enterTextEdit(el){
      editingEl = el;
      textEditBatch = captureBatch([el]);
      el.contentEditable = 'true';
      el.spellcheck = false;
      el.classList.add('cv-editing-text');
      el.focus();
      // Cursor starts at the end of the existing text, so typing adds on
      // rather than replacing what's already there.
      var range = document.createRange();
      range.selectNodeContents(el);
      range.collapse(false);
      var s = window.getSelection();
      s.removeAllRanges();
      s.addRange(range);
    }
    function exitTextEdit(){
      if (!editingEl) return;
      var el = editingEl;
      editingEl = null;
      el.contentEditable = 'false';
      el.classList.remove('cv-editing-text');
      saveText(el);
      if (textEditBatch){ commitBatch(textEditBatch); textEditBatch = null; }
    }
    function insertLineBreak(){
      // Not a hand-rolled Range insertion: browsers get ambiguous about
      // caret placement when a <br> ends up as the last child (the next
      // typed character can land BEFORE it instead of after) — the native
      // command already handles that quirk correctly, since browsers use
      // this same routine internally for shift+Enter in real editors.
      if (!document.execCommand('insertLineBreak')){
        document.execCommand('insertHTML', false, '<br>');
      }
    }

    // ---- hover outline (shows the whole tile — what a single click grabs) ----
    root.addEventListener('mousemove', function(e){
      if (dragging || editingEl) return;
      var hit = e.target.closest(EDITABLE);
      var t = hit ? (hit.closest('.pdp-cmp__card') || hit) : null;
      if (lastHover && lastHover !== t) lastHover.classList.remove('cv-hover');
      if (t && t !== sel) t.classList.add('cv-hover');
      lastHover = t;
    });
    var lastHover = null;
    root.addEventListener('mouseleave', function(){ if (lastHover){ lastHover.classList.remove('cv-hover'); lastHover = null; } });

    // Swallow native clicks (links, the <select> dropdown, etc.) while editing.
    root.addEventListener('click', function(e){ if (e.target.closest(EDITABLE)){ e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation(); } }, true);

    // ---- drag: move ----
    var dragging = null;
    function onDown(e){
      // A field is currently being typed into: clicks inside it just place
      // the cursor (native behavior); clicks anywhere else save + close it
      // before doing anything else, so a click on the toolbar or another
      // tile never loses an in-progress edit.
      if (editingEl && !editingEl.contains(e.target)) exitTextEdit();
      if (e.target.closest('.cv-tb, .cv-panel')) return;
      if (editingEl) return;
      var handle = e.target.closest('.cv-h');
      if (handle && sel){ startResize(e, handle.dataset.corner); return; }
      var hit = e.target.closest(EDITABLE);
      if (!hit || !root.contains(hit)){ deselect(); return; }
      // Canva model: single click grabs the whole tile; double-click drills
      // into the exact element under the cursor (text / image / icon); and once
      // something is drilled into, pressing on it again keeps it selected so it
      // can be dragged (instead of snapping back to the whole tile).
      var card = hit.closest('.pdp-cmp__card');
      var drilledOnSel = sel && sel !== card && (sel === hit || sel.contains(hit));
      var t;
      if (!card) t = hit;              // heading / selector — direct
      else if (e.detail >= 2) t = hit; // double-click drills to the exact element
      else if (drilledOnSel) t = sel;  // keep a drilled child selected so it can be dragged
      else t = card;                   // single click grabs the whole tile

      // A click that doesn't turn into a drag, landing on a text box that's
      // ALREADY selected (i.e. this is a repeat click on it, not the click
      // that first drilled into it), starts typing — same effect as
      // pressing Enter. This has to be a *second* click on an already-
      // selected text box rather than any click, or double-clicking to
      // drill/select a caption for dragging would get hijacked into typing
      // every time, same bug as before.
      var wasSelected = (sel === t);

      e.preventDefault();
      select(t);
      if (lastHover){ lastHover.classList.remove('cv-hover'); lastHover = null; }
      var sc = cumScale(t), st = stateOf(t);
      dragging = {el:t, mode:'move', sx:e.clientX, sy:e.clientY, dx0:st.dx, dy0:st.dy, s0:st.s, scx:sc.sx, scy:sc.sy, moved:false, wasSelected:wasSelected, batch:captureBatch([t])};
    }
    function startResize(e, corner){
      e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
      var c = centerOf(sel), st = stateOf(sel);
      var d0 = Math.hypot(e.clientX - c.x, e.clientY - c.y) || 1;
      dragging = {el:sel, mode:'scale', d0:d0, s0:st.s, dx0:st.dx, dy0:st.dy, cx:c.x, cy:c.y, batch:captureBatch([sel])};
    }
    function onMove(e){
      if (!dragging) return;
      var d = dragging, st = stateOf(d.el);
      if (d.mode === 'move'){
        if (Math.abs(e.clientX - d.sx) > 3 || Math.abs(e.clientY - d.sy) > 3) d.moved = true;
        st.dx = d.dx0 + (e.clientX - d.sx) / d.scx;
        st.dy = d.dy0 + (e.clientY - d.sy) / d.scy;
      } else {
        var dist = Math.hypot(e.clientX - d.cx, e.clientY - d.cy);
        var ns = d.s0 * (dist / d.d0);
        st.s = Math.max(0.15, Math.min(10, ns));
      }
      saveState(d.el, st);
      positionBox();
    }
    function onUp(){
      if (dragging && !dragging.moved && dragging.wasSelected && dragging.el.__cvTextEditable && dragging.el !== editingEl){
        enterTextEdit(dragging.el);
      }
      if (dragging && dragging.batch) commitBatch(dragging.batch);
      dragging = null;
    }

    document.addEventListener('mousedown', onDown, true);
    document.addEventListener('mousemove', onMove, true);
    document.addEventListener('mouseup', onUp, true);

    // ---- touch: the phone equivalent of the mouse flow above ----
    // The desktop path (mouse) is left exactly as-is; this is a separate,
    // additive set of handlers so nothing about the proven desktop editor
    // changes. On a touch-only phone only these fire; on desktop only the
    // mouse ones do.
    //
    // Model (a finger can't hover, right-click, scroll-wheel, or press
    // arrow keys, so it can't be identical):
    //   • tap a tile                → select it (whole tile)
    //   • tap again / double-tap    → drill into the image/icon/caption under it
    //   • double-tap a caption      → start typing (on-screen keyboard)
    //   • drag the SELECTED element → move it (it alone is touch-action:none)
    //   • drag anywhere else        → the page scrolls normally
    //   • drag a corner handle      → resize
    // Everything commits to the same undo/localStorage/"Copy layout" as the
    // mouse path — it's the same state, just a different input.
    var pendingTap = null; // a touch that may become a tap (select) or a scroll
    var lastTap = null;    // {el, t} for double-tap detection
    var pinch = null;      // an active two-finger resize gesture
    function findTouch(list, id){
      for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) if (list[i].identifier === id) return list[i];
      return null;
    }
    function makeMoveT(el, cx, cy, wasSelected, id){
      var sc = cumScale(el), st = stateOf(el);
      return {el:el, mode:'move', id:id, sx:cx, sy:cy, dx0:st.dx, dy0:st.dy, s0:st.s,
              scx:sc.sx, scy:sc.sy, moved:false, wasSelected:wasSelected, batch:captureBatch([el])};
    }
    function startResizeT(cx, cy, corner, id){
      var c = centerOf(sel), st = stateOf(sel);
      var d0 = Math.hypot(cx - c.x, cy - c.y) || 1;
      dragging = {el:sel, mode:'scale', id:id, d0:d0, s0:st.s, dx0:st.dx, dy0:st.dy, cx:c.x, cy:c.y, batch:captureBatch([sel])};
    }
    function endDragging(){
      if (dragging && !dragging.moved && dragging.wasSelected && dragging.el.__cvTextEditable && dragging.el !== editingEl){
        enterTextEdit(dragging.el);
      }
      if (dragging && dragging.batch) commitBatch(dragging.batch);
      dragging = null;
    }
    function startPinch(t0, t1){
      pinch = {id1:t0.identifier, id2:t1.identifier,
               d0: Math.hypot(t1.clientX - t0.clientX, t1.clientY - t0.clientY) || 1,
               s0: stateOf(sel).s, batch: captureBatch([sel])};
    }
    function endPinch(){
      if (pinch && pinch.batch) commitBatch(pinch.batch);
      pinch = null;
    }
    function resolveTap(p){
      var hit = p.el, card = p.card, now = Date.now();
      var dbl = lastTap && lastTap.el === hit && (now - lastTap.t) < 340;
      lastTap = {el:hit, t:now};
      var t;
      if (!card) t = hit;                       // heading / selector
      else if (dbl){
        // double-tap a caption → straight into typing; anything else → drill
        if (isTextEditable(hit)){ select(hit); enterTextEdit(hit); return; }
        t = hit;
      }
      else if (sel && sel !== card && (sel === hit || sel.contains(hit))) t = sel; // keep drilled child
      else t = card;                            // single tap → whole tile
      // a plain repeat tap on an already-selected caption → type
      if (sel === t && isTextEditable(t) && !dbl){ enterTextEdit(t); return; }
      select(t);
    }
    function onTouchStart(e){
      if (e.touches.length > 1){
        // A second finger landing — whatever single-finger gesture was in
        // progress ends cleanly right here (committed, not abandoned mid-
        // motion) and a fresh two-finger pinch-resize takes over. Without
        // this, a stray extra finger (e.g. a resting thumb) mid-drag would
        // leave touches[0] pointing at a DIFFERENT finger than the one
        // actually being tracked, which is what made a dragged image
        // suddenly jump/"fly" — every gesture below is now tracked by its
        // own touch identifier instead of always trusting touches[0].
        pendingTap = null;
        endDragging();
        if (sel) { e.preventDefault(); startPinch(e.touches[0], e.touches[1]); }
        return;
      }
      var pt = e.touches[0];
      var target = document.elementFromPoint(pt.clientX, pt.clientY) || e.target;
      if (editingEl && !editingEl.contains(target)) exitTextEdit();
      if (target.closest('.cv-tb, .cv-panel')) return; // toolbar taps behave natively
      if (editingEl) return;
      var handle = target.closest('.cv-h');
      if (handle && sel){ e.preventDefault(); startResizeT(pt.clientX, pt.clientY, handle.dataset.corner, pt.identifier); return; }
      var hit = target.closest(EDITABLE);
      if (!hit || !root.contains(hit)){ pendingTap = null; deselect(); return; }
      pendingTap = {el:hit, card:hit.closest('.pdp-cmp__card'), x:pt.clientX, y:pt.clientY, id:pt.identifier};
    }
    function onTouchMove(e){
      if (pinch){
        var pt0 = findTouch(e.touches, pinch.id1), pt1 = findTouch(e.touches, pinch.id2);
        if (!pt0 || !pt1) return; // one of the two tracked fingers isn't in this event — ignore, wait for touchend
        var dist = Math.hypot(pt1.clientX - pt0.clientX, pt1.clientY - pt0.clientY);
        var st = stateOf(sel);
        st.s = Math.max(0.15, Math.min(10, pinch.s0 * (dist / pinch.d0)));
        saveState(sel, st); positionBox();
        e.preventDefault();
        return;
      }
      if (dragging){
        var p = findTouch(e.touches, dragging.id); if (!p) return; // not the tracked finger
        var d = dragging, st2 = stateOf(d.el);
        if (d.mode === 'move'){
          if (Math.abs(p.clientX - d.sx) > 3 || Math.abs(p.clientY - d.sy) > 3) d.moved = true;
          st2.dx = d.dx0 + (p.clientX - d.sx) / d.scx;
          st2.dy = d.dy0 + (p.clientY - d.sy) / d.scy;
        } else {
          var dist2 = Math.hypot(p.clientX - d.cx, p.clientY - d.cy);
          st2.s = Math.max(0.15, Math.min(10, d.s0 * (dist2 / d.d0)));
        }
        saveState(d.el, st2); positionBox();
        e.preventDefault();
        return;
      }
      if (pendingTap){
        var q = findTouch(e.touches, pendingTap.id); if (!q) return;
        if (Math.abs(q.clientX - pendingTap.x) > 8 || Math.abs(q.clientY - pendingTap.y) > 8){
          // moved past the tap threshold: if it's on the current selection,
          // this is a move-drag; otherwise it's a page scroll — let it go.
          if (sel && (sel === pendingTap.el || sel.contains(pendingTap.el))){
            dragging = makeMoveT(sel, q.clientX, q.clientY, true, pendingTap.id);
            e.preventDefault();
          }
          pendingTap = null;
        }
      }
    }
    function onTouchEnd(e){
      if (pinch){
        // Below two fingers again — done, whether that's this ending touch
        // or a third finger that was never tracked lifting.
        if (e.touches.length < 2) endPinch();
        return;
      }
      if (pendingTap){ resolveTap(pendingTap); pendingTap = null; }
      if (dragging && !findTouch(e.touches, dragging.id)) endDragging();
    }
    document.addEventListener('touchstart', onTouchStart, {passive:false, capture:true});
    document.addEventListener('touchmove', onTouchMove, {passive:false, capture:true});
    document.addEventListener('touchend', onTouchEnd, {passive:false, capture:true});
    document.addEventListener('touchcancel', onTouchEnd, {passive:false, capture:true});

    window.addEventListener('scroll', positionBox, true);
    window.addEventListener('resize', positionBox);

    // ---- wheel to resize the selected element ----
    // A scroll gesture fires many wheel events in a burst — treat the whole
    // burst as one undo step (capture once at the start, commit once
    // ~400ms after the wheel goes quiet) instead of one per tick.
    var wheelBatch = null, wheelIdleTimer = null;
    document.addEventListener('wheel', function(e){
      if (!sel || editingEl) return;
      var r = sel.getBoundingClientRect();
      if (e.clientX < r.left || e.clientX > r.right || e.clientY < r.top || e.clientY > r.bottom) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      if (!wheelBatch) wheelBatch = captureBatch([sel]);
      clearTimeout(wheelIdleTimer);
      wheelIdleTimer = setTimeout(function(){ commitBatch(wheelBatch); wheelBatch = null; }, 400);
      var st = stateOf(sel);
      st.s = Math.max(0.15, Math.min(10, st.s * (e.deltaY < 0 ? 1.05 : 0.9524)));
      saveState(sel, st); positionBox();
    }, {passive:false});

    // ---- arrow-key nudge (and typing, when a caption is being edited) ----
    document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){
      if (editingEl){
        if (e.key === 'Enter'){
          e.preventDefault();
          insertLineBreak();
          saveText(editingEl);
        } else if (e.key === 'Escape'){
          e.preventDefault();
          exitTextEdit();
        }
        return; // every other key (letters, backspace, arrow-to-move-cursor...) behaves natively
      }
      if (!sel) return;
      // A selected caption is still draggable by holding the mouse on it
      // (same as any other selected element) — Enter is what switches it
      // into typing, so the two never compete for the same click.
      if (e.key === 'Enter' && isTextEditable(sel)){ e.preventDefault(); enterTextEdit(sel); return; }
      // Backspace/Delete on a SELECTED (not currently-typed-into) text box
      // clears it — same idea as pressing Enter to type, just the opposite:
      // one keypress, not held down, no confirm dialog, because it's a
      // single undo-able step either way.
      if ((e.key === 'Backspace' || e.key === 'Delete') && isTextEditable(sel)){
        e.preventDefault();
        var delBatch = captureBatch([sel]);
        sel.innerHTML = '';
        var delSt = stateOf(sel);
        delSt.text = '';
        saveState(sel, delSt);
        commitBatch(delBatch);
        positionBox();
        return;
      }
      if (e.key === 'Escape'){ deselect(); return; }
      // Holding an arrow key fires many keydown events — coalesce a whole
      // hold into one undo step the same way the wheel-resize burst does.
      var step = e.shiftKey ? 10 : 1, st = stateOf(sel), moved = true;
      if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') st.dx -= step; else if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') st.dx += step;
      else if (e.key === 'ArrowUp') st.dy -= step; else if (e.key === 'ArrowDown') st.dy += step;
      else moved = false;
      if (moved){
        e.preventDefault();
        if (!nudgeBatch) nudgeBatch = captureBatch([sel]);
        clearTimeout(nudgeIdleTimer);
        nudgeIdleTimer = setTimeout(function(){ commitBatch(nudgeBatch); nudgeBatch = null; }, 400);
        saveState(sel, st);
        positionBox();
      }
    });
    var nudgeBatch = null, nudgeIdleTimer = null;

    // Live-save while typing (covers the case where a click elsewhere is
    // the very first event caught, so nothing is lost between keystrokes
    // and the eventual exit-save).
    root.addEventListener('input', function(e){
      if (editingEl && e.target === editingEl) saveText(editingEl);
    });

    // ---- align: snap small accidental drift back to perfect (tiles only) ----
    // `offsetLeft`/`offsetTop` reflect a tile's actual CSS Grid cell and are
    // untouched by our own transform, no matter how far it's been dragged —
    // so the 6 tiles' own offsetLeft/offsetTop are always exactly the 6 real
    // grid slots, even mid-rearrange. That means Align can snap a dragged
    // tile to whichever slot it's now CLOSEST to (not just back to its own
    // original slot) — so swapping two tiles by roughly dragging them into
    // each other's spot, then clicking Align, locks them exactly into
    // place instead of only correcting drift from their old spot.
    //
    // Align ONLY ever touches a tile's own position/size — never anything
    // INSIDE a tile (images, icons, text). It used to also snap small
    // horizontal drift on those, but that meant a deliberate small nudge
    // (e.g. a photo shifted 6px on purpose) kept getting silently reverted
    // every time Align ran. Once something is placed inside a tile, it
    // stays exactly where it's put — only the tile itself gets straightened.
    // Click "Align" for a normal-size correction (up to 14px of drift);
    // hold Shift and click for a bigger correction (up to 40px). Anything
    // drifted further than that is left alone as a deliberate move.
    function nearestTileSlot(x, y, tiles){
      var best = null, bestDist = Infinity;
      tiles.forEach(function(t){
        var d = Math.hypot(x - t.offsetLeft, y - t.offsetTop);
        if (d < bestDist){ bestDist = d; best = t; }
      });
      return best;
    }
    function align(threshold){
      var wantedTargets = sel ? [sel] : els;
      var tileTargets = wantedTargets.filter(function(el){ return el.matches('.pdp-cmp__card'); });
      var textTargets = wantedTargets.filter(function(el){ return el.__cvAlignH; });
      var tiles = els.filter(function(el){ return el.matches('.pdp-cmp__card'); });
      var batch = captureBatch(tileTargets.concat(textTargets));
      var n = 0;
      tileTargets.forEach(function(el){
        var st = stateOf(el), changed = false;
        var curX = el.offsetLeft + st.dx, curY = el.offsetTop + st.dy;
        var slot = nearestTileSlot(curX, curY, tiles);
        if (slot){
          var wantDx = slot.offsetLeft - el.offsetLeft, wantDy = slot.offsetTop - el.offsetTop;
          var errX = curX - slot.offsetLeft, errY = curY - slot.offsetTop;
          if ((st.dx !== wantDx || st.dy !== wantDy) && Math.abs(errX) <= threshold && Math.abs(errY) <= threshold){
            st.dx = wantDx; st.dy = wantDy; changed = true;
          }
        }
        if (st.s !== 1 && Math.abs(st.s - 1) <= threshold / 400){ st.s = 1; changed = true; }
        if (changed){ saveState(el, st); n++; }
      });
      // Text boxes only ever get straightened left/right — small drift
      // only, same rule as a tile — never resized or moved vertically by
      // Align (their vertical spot is set by their own CSS on purpose).
      textTargets.forEach(function(el){
        var st = stateOf(el), changed = false;
        if (st.dx !== 0 && Math.abs(st.dx) <= threshold){ st.dx = 0; changed = true; }
        if (changed){ saveState(el, st); n++; }
      });
      commitBatch(batch);
      positionBox();
      return n;
    }

    // ---- export payload for "lock it" ----
    function exportCode(){
      var out = [];
      els.forEach(function(el){
        var s = layout[el.__cvKey];
        if (!s) return;
        var hasTransform = s.dx || s.dy || (s.s && s.s !== 1);
        var hasText = s.text != null;
        if (!hasTransform && !hasText) return;
        var item = { sel: '.pdp-cmp>' + el.__cvKey, kind: label(el), dx: s.dx||0, dy: s.dy||0, s: s.s||1, base: el.__cvBase || 'none' };
        if (hasText) item.text = s.text;
        out.push(item);
      });
      return JSON.stringify({ v:1, note:'Voltical compare-grid layout — desktop', items: out }, null, 2);
    }

    // ---- toolbar ----
    var tb = document.createElement('div'); tb.className = 'cv-tb';
    var hintText = coarse
      ? 'Tap a tile to select · drag the selected tile to move · double-tap what’s inside to grab it (or a caption to type) · pinch or drag a corner to resize · drag elsewhere to scroll'
      : 'Click a tile · double-click to grab what’s inside · drag to move · corner or scroll to resize · arrows nudge · Enter types into a selected caption · Backspace deletes selected text';
    tb.innerHTML =
      '<span class="cv-tb__dot"></span><span class="cv-tb__title">Canva mode</span>' +
      '<span class="cv-tb__hint">' + hintText + '</span>' +
      '<button class="cv-btn" data-cv="undo" title="Undo the last move, resize, type, delete, Align, or Reset.">Undo</button>' +
      '<button class="cv-btn" data-cv="align" title="Straighten tiles onto the grid and text boxes left/right. Leaves images and icons alone. Shift+click for a bigger correction.">Align</button>' +
      '<button class="cv-btn" data-cv="reset-sel">Reset one</button>' +
      '<button class="cv-btn" data-cv="reset-all">Reset all</button>' +
      '<button class="cv-btn cv-btn--go" data-cv="copy">Copy layout</button>' +
      '<button class="cv-btn" data-cv="done">Done</button>';
    document.body.appendChild(tb);

    // ---- export panel ----
    var panel = document.createElement('div'); panel.className = 'cv-panel';
    panel.innerHTML =
      '<div class="cv-panel__card">' +
        '<div class="cv-panel__head"><b>Layout code</b><button class="cv-btn" data-cv="close">Close</button></div>' +
        '<textarea readonly spellcheck="false"></textarea>' +
        '<div class="cv-panel__foot"><span class="cv-panel__note">Copied to your clipboard. Paste this to Claude and say “lock it”.</span>' +
        '<button class="cv-btn cv-btn--go" data-cv="copy2">Copy again</button></div>' +
      '</div>';
    document.body.appendChild(panel);
    var ta = panel.querySelector('textarea');

    function copyToClipboard(text){ try { navigator.clipboard.writeText(text); } catch(e){ try { ta.focus(); ta.select(); document.execCommand('copy'); } catch(_){} } }

    tb.addEventListener('click', function(e){
      var b = e.target.closest('[data-cv]'); if (!b) return;
      var a = b.dataset.cv;
      if (a === 'undo'){ undo(); }
      else if (a === 'align'){ align(e.shiftKey ? 40 : 14); }
      else if (a === 'reset-sel' && sel){
        var resetBatch = captureBatch([sel]);
        var keepText = stateOf(sel).text;
        saveState(sel, {dx:0, dy:0, s:1, text:keepText});
        commitBatch(resetBatch);
        positionBox();
      }
      else if (a === 'reset-all'){
        if (confirm('Reset every tile, image and text back to its original position? (typed caption edits are kept)')){
          var resetAllBatch = captureBatch(els.filter(function(el){ return layout[el.__cvKey]; }));
          Object.keys(layout).forEach(function(k){
            layout[k] = layout[k].text != null ? {dx:0, dy:0, s:1, text:layout[k].text} : undefined;
            if (layout[k] === undefined) delete layout[k];
          });
          ls(false, LKEY, JSON.stringify(layout));
          commitBatch(resetAllBatch);
          els.forEach(applyState);
          deselect();
        }
      }
      else if (a === 'copy'){ ta.value = exportCode(); copyToClipboard(ta.value); panel.classList.add('is-open'); }
      else if (a === 'done'){
        rm('volt-canva-on');
        var search = location.search.replace(/([?&])edit=\d+/g, '').replace(/^&/, '?').replace(/^\?$/, '');
        location.href = location.pathname + search + location.hash;
      }
    });
    panel.addEventListener('click', function(e){
      var b = e.target.closest('[data-cv]');
      if (b && b.dataset.cv === 'close'){ panel.classList.remove('is-open'); return; }
      if (b && b.dataset.cv === 'copy2'){ copyToClipboard(ta.value); return; }
      if (e.target === panel) panel.classList.remove('is-open');
    });
  }

  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', start);
  else start();
})();
</script>
